      "text": "To find the new class mean score after all 36 students have taken the test, we need to determine the total score for all 36 students and then find the average of these scores.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total score of the 30 students who took the test the first time. The mean score of these 30 students is 72%. Therefore, the total score for these 30 students is:\n\\[\n30 \\times 72 = 2160\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the total score of the 6 students who took the test the second time. The mean score of these 6 students is 78%. Therefore, the total score for these 6 students is:\n\\[\n6 \\times 78 = 468\n\\]\n\nNow, we find the combined total score for all 36 students by adding the total scores of the two groups:\n\\[\n2160 + 468 = 2628\n\\]\n\nTo find the new class mean, we divide the combined total score by the total number of students:\n\\[\n\\frac{2628}{36} = 73\n\\]\n\nThus, the new class mean is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{73}\n\\]",
